{% macro general() %}
- Make sure not to add trailing white spaces to lines
- When changing existing file (those with FILENAME information):
    - Ensure that output also contains FILENAME information. Replace spaces in filename with dashes.
    - Only return files that where changed but then return entire changed file, including the parts that have not changed.
    - If files are meant for deletion, write as first line "FILENAME: DELETE path/to/file". Don't add any content.
    - FILENAME information always is first line. File name never contains spaces, e.g.
          FILENAME: path/to/this-is-the-file.md
        Actual file content goes here
- Answer in same language as question was asked. If hard to tell, default to English.
- Date format: dd.MM.yyyy, e.g. 01.12.2035
- Never add TODOs
{% endmacro %}
